# Next.js / React / TypeScript project-rule (template)

Replace `{{APP_NAME}}` and path aliases (`@/`). Assumes **App Router** (`app/`). **Keep only one tier** in the active rule.

---

## How to choose a tier

| Tier | When to use |
|------|-------------|
| **Small** | Landing + few pages, marketing site, internal dashboard |
| **Medium** | Production SaaS web app, authenticated product UI |
| **Big** | Enterprise web, strict SEO/compliance, monorepo, edge + multi-region |

---

## Tier: Small project

### S1. Scope

- **App Router** with **Server Components** by default; **`use client`** only where needed (interactivity, browser APIs).
- **Co-locate** components with routes or a single `components/` folder.

### S2. Layout

```
app/
├── layout.tsx
├── page.tsx
├── (routes...)/
components/
lib/
public/
```

### S3. Data fetching

- **`fetch`** in Server Components with **`next: { revalidate }`** or **`cache: 'no-store'`** as appropriate.
- **Env**: `process.env` — **only** `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` exposed to client.

### S4. Styling

- **Tailwind CSS** or **CSS Modules** — one primary system; **consistent** spacing scale.

### S5. Forms and validation

- **Server Actions** or **Route Handlers** with **Zod** validation for mutations.

### S6. Quality

- **`next build`** succeeds; **ESLint** `next/core-web-vitals`.
- **Basic** **metadata** (`metadata` export) for SEO on public pages.

### S7. Checklist (small)

- [ ] No secrets in client bundles.
- [ ] Error UI (`error.tsx`) and not-found (`not-found.tsx`) where product needs polish.
- [ ] Images use **`next/image`** when from remote allowlist.

---

## Tier: Medium project

### M1. Architecture

- **Feature folders** under `app/` or parallel `features/<name>/` with **ui**, **actions**, **schemas`:

```
features/
├── billing/
│   ├── components/
│   ├── actions.ts
│   └── schema.ts
├── auth/
core/
├── db/                    # Prisma / Drizzle client
├── auth/
└── utils/
```

- **Server vs client** boundary explicit: shared **types** in `types/`; no server-only imports in client components.

### M2. TypeScript and React

- **Strict** TS; **React 19** / **18** patterns per project — **no** deprecated lifecycle in new code.
- **Hooks** rules enforced by ESLint; **keys** stable on lists.

### M3. Auth and session

- **Auth.js (NextAuth)** or **Clerk** / **Auth0** — **one** provider pattern; **session** access only through documented helpers.
- **Middleware** for route protection; **CSRF** considered for cookie sessions.

### M4. Data layer

- **Prisma** or **Drizzle** with **migrations**; **repository** or **dao** optional thin layer over ORM for testability.
- **React Query / TanStack Query** for **client** data that needs caching/refetch (when using client fetchers).

### M5. API routes

- **Route Handlers** (`app/api/.../route.ts`) return **typed** JSON; **Zod** parse **body** and **query**.
- **Rate limit** sensitive endpoints (Upstash, Redis).

### M6. Performance

- **`loading.tsx`** and **Suspense** boundaries for perceived performance.
- **Dynamic imports** for heavy client-only widgets.
- **Analytics** (Vercel, PostHog, etc.) loaded with **privacy** in mind.

### M7. Testing

- **Vitest** + **React Testing Library** for units; **Playwright** for **E2E** critical paths in CI.

### M8. i18n and a11y

- **next-intl** or equivalent if multi-language; **focus management** on route change where needed.
- **Semantic HTML**; **labels** on form controls.

### M9. Deploy environments, error tracking, and feature flags (medium baseline)

Production-oriented medium web apps treat these as **standard**.

- **Environments (`dev` / `staging` / `prod`)**: **Vercel** preview vs production (or self-hosted equivalents) with **separate** env vars in the host dashboard. Use **`VERCEL_ENV`** / **`NODE_ENV`** plus named vars (`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`, server-only `API_SECRET`) — **never** ship prod-only secrets to **preview**. Document **local** `.env.local` vs **CI**; **branch** → **staging** mapping when using preview deployments.
- **Crash and performance**: **Sentry** (or **OpenTelemetry** + vendor) for **server** and **browser** with **release** / **git SHA**; **Web Vitals** reporting (Vercel Analytics, Speed Insights, or custom). Review **staging/preview** error and **LCP/INP** regressions before promoting to **production**.
- **Feature flags**: **LaunchDarkly**, **Vercel Flags**, **PostHog**, **GrowthBook**, etc. — **document** flag keys, defaults per environment, owners; **server-side** evaluation for sensitive behavior; **cleanup** stale flags.

### M10. Checklist (medium)

- [ ] Server/client boundaries documented for new features.
- [ ] Auth checks on all protected server actions and routes.
- [ ] CI: lint, typecheck, test, build.
- [ ] CSP headers or middleware security headers configured for prod.
- [ ] **Environments**: verified on **preview/staging** before prod; no prod secrets in client bundles.
- [ ] **Error / Web Vitals**: release tracking enabled; PII policy followed in client events.
- [ ] **Feature flags**: new flags documented with owner and removal plan.

---

## Tier: Big project

### B1. Monorepo and design system

- **Turborepo** / **Nx**: `apps/web`, `packages/ui`, `packages/config-eslint`.
- **Design system** package versioned; **visual regression** (Chromatic, etc.) if brand-critical.

### B2. Rendering strategy

- Document **per-route** choice: **static**, **ISR**, **dynamic**, **edge** — **no** accidental full dynamic on marketing pages.
- **`unstable_cache`** / **`fetch` cache** semantics reviewed for **stale** data risk.

### B3. Observability and reliability

- **Builds on medium baseline** (§M9): **OpenTelemetry** end-to-end where required; **formal** release health gates on errors and **Core Web Vitals**; **feature-flag** rollout playbooks with **rollback** tied to metrics.

### B4. Security and compliance

- **Content Security Policy** strict; **Subresource Integrity** where applicable.
- **GDPR/CCPA**: consent banners, **data export** flows if product requires.
- **Penetration test** remediation backlog tracked.

### B5. SEO and international

- **`sitemap.ts`**, **`robots.ts`**, **hreflang** for multi-region.
- **Structured data** where product benefits.

### B6. Checklist (big)

- [ ] Performance budgets (LCP, CLS) monitored per release.
- [ ] Incident response and rollback for deployments.
- [ ] Accessibility audit cadence (WCAG target documented).
- [ ] ADRs for rendering, auth, and data-fetch strategy changes.

